# Castafiore - Session Log

## 2026-08-28 — Fix: next/prev loops on same song (icons + Bluetooth, not swipe)
- Symptom: pressing next/prev (full-screen transport / notification / Bluetooth) sometimes plays
  the same song from the start 3-5× before advancing; swipe never does.
- Root cause: commit `d8ffc98` (KISS refactor) changed native `setIndex` from fire-and-forget
  load + immediate dispatch to `await loadSong` + deferred dispatch. During the load window
  `global.song.index` stays stale → a re-trigger (natural `PlaybackQueueEnded` near song end,
  Bluetooth double event, fast double-tap) issues a second `load()` of the same track → the
  song restarts until the deferred dispatch lands. Verified the KotlinAudio fork only emits
  `AudioPlayerState.ENDED` (→ `PlaybackQueueEnded`) on genuine end of playback, and `MusicService`
  emits QueueEnded on every `ENDED` transition → the cascade.
- "Not swipe": swipes land mid-song (no ENDED, single invocation); icons/Bluetooth are pressed
  at/near song end and double-fire.
- Fix: `playerCore.setIndex` dedupes in-flight loads of the same track id (`loadingKey`,
  try/finally cleared) — a repeat request for an already-loading track only dispatches state.
  One shared chokepoint covers local/cast/upnp/web auto-advance routes
  (`servicePlayback.PlaybackQueueEnded`, cast `onMediaPlaybackEnded`, upnp `TRACK_ENDED`, web `ended`).
- eslint clean. Plan: `plans/fix-next-prev-looping.md`. TODO #29. On-device verify pending.
- Not fixed (known, benign): (a) different-target rapid double-skip still briefly races two
  distinct loads (pre-existing `load()` semantics, not a loop); (b) repeat-ON transient restart
  during the window before `setRepeat('next')` lands. UpNext branch unaffected (loads directly).

