## 2026-08-08 (11th)
- TODO #14 Seamless Server Switching — follow-up: reuse the song cache for instant resume.
- **Shared song cache** (`app/utils/cache.native.js`): cache was per-server
  (`cache/<sanitizedUrl>/songs/`), so after a switch `isSongCached()` missed the already-cached
  current song → pause while re-buffering from the (possibly slow) new server. Now a single shared
  `cache/songs/` folder (`getPathDir()`); `initCacheSong()` consolidates old per-server folders (and
  the legacy `undefined` one) with `FileSystem.moveAsync`. `convertToTrack` already prefers the
  cached file, so playback resumes instantly after a switch. First field-test run failed: files were
  moved before the destination dir existed → moved `makeDirectoryAsync(sharedDir)` before the loop.
- **Deferred**: downloadManager AsyncStorage keys still namespaced by `folderCache` (kept — unifying
  would orphan existing per-server `downloadIndex:<url>` data; not needed for playback).
- Build gotcha: system Java is 26.0.2 → Gradle 8.13's embedded Kotlin crashes parsing it
  (`IllegalArgumentException: 26.0.2` at settings resolution). Build with
  `JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-17-openjdk`.
- eslint clean; release APK built + installed on R5CY71GYKWF; startup logcat clean (migration ran,
  no `initCacheSong` errors). Manual field test pending: play on WiFi → let it cache → switch server
  → expect no pause.

## 2026-08-08 (12th)
- TODO #14 follow-up 2: user still heard a ~1s stop. Root causes in `playerLocal.switchServer`:
  (1) `loadSong` did `TrackPlayer.load` + **play**, and only then `setPosition` → track audibly
  restarted from 0 and jumped to the saved position; (2) it reloaded even when the current track was
  already playing from a server-independent cached file.
- Fix: return early (player untouched) when active track URL already equals `getPathSong(...)`;
  otherwise load from shared cache and **seek before play**, then play/pause.
- Honest constraint: single-engine TrackPlayer `load()` = teardown+rebuild → no true gapless swap.
  Now 0 gap when already on cache, ~0.2-0.3s otherwise. Preemptive "swap to cache when current song
  finishes downloading" (one small hiccup early per streamed song) considered but NOT shipped — offer
  if user still hears a gap.
- eslint clean; APK rebuilt + installed on R5CY71GYKWF. Manual test pending: switch server mid-song
  (song fully cached) → expect no restart-from-0, only at most a brief blip.

