## 2026-08-06 (9th)
- Queue view polish (TODO #1 follow-up). Plan: `plans/queue-dnd.md`.
- Pinned **"Now playing"** row at the top of the QUEUE view (above "Up next" and "Queue"), non-draggable
  (mobile: `SongItem` with playing indicator; desktop: right-aligned `QueueRow` with overlay). New i18n key.
- **Cross-section drag-and-drop**: `QueueDragRow.js` rewritten into `QueueDragProvider` + `QueueDragRow`.
  One manager for both lists — measures each list via `measureInWindow`, resolves the drop target from the
  absolute finger position vs list bounds, edge-autoscrolls the active list (queue list `viewport` now
  wired via `onLayout`; it was never set before, so queue autoscroll never engaged), and **springs sibling
  rows to ±rowHeight to open a live gap** while the dragged row is lifted (elevation + background).
  Drop → new `moveTrack` util → `moveUpNext`/`moveInQueue` (same list) or new reducer cases
  `moveUpNextToQueue`/`moveQueueToUpNext` (cross list; the latter ignores `from === song.index`, so the
  current song can't be dropped into "Up next"; the UI also clamps the current row's target to the queue).
- Desktop rows now render a drag handle (`QueueRow`); previously the raw `Pressable` rows ignored the
  injected `handle` prop, so desktop had no drag.
- **Follow-up fixes** (after device smoke test):
  - **Crash on drag**: `startDrag` called `measureInWindow` on the `FlatList` ref, which doesn't expose it
    ("TypeError: undefined is not a function"). Now each list is wrapped in a `View` (`queueBox`/`upNextBox`)
    and the provider measures those (guarded with `?.`). The up-next section header was moved outside the
    measured box so the box frame aligns with the first row.
  - **Current song removed from the queue list** (user request — it's already the pinned "Now playing"):
    the queue `FlatList` now renders `queueItems = queue minus song.index` (display-level; the full queue
    stays the source of truth). Queue display indices are mapped to real queue indices for
    `moveTrack`/`setIndex`/long-press options; open-view scroll targets the first upcoming song
    (display index `song.index`, clamped). The now-unneeded `crossBlock` clamp was dropped (the reducer
    guard `from === song.index` remains as a safety net).
- eslint clean; APK rebuilt (40s) + installed on R5CY71GYKWF; launch + drag smoke verified (no crash).
- **Follow-up fixes (round 2)** — device smoke test found drag behaving wrong ("songs go nowhere") and the
  lifted row disappearing:
  - **Drag rewrite** (`QueueDrag.js`): window-coordinate measurement is unreliable inside a `Modal`, so the
    provider now computes everything relative to the shared container — both lists are direct children of one
    parent, their `onLayout` `boxY`/`boxH` + the gesture `dy` resolve the drop target, no `measureInWindow`.
    Region detection only engages "Up next" when that box actually exists (a previously absent box captured
    drops); cross-section gap = trailing rows (`index >= targetIndex`) shift `+rowHeight` (the old code
    compared indices across lists); same-list gaps shift per from/target relationship; desktop's bottom-aligned
    queue gets a `bottomPad` correction.
  - **Row disappearing**: lifted row dropped `elevation`/`zIndex` (translateY inside a clipped FlatList on
    Android made it vanish) — lifted styling is now just `backgroundColor`. Spring uses `useNativeDriver: false`.
- **Refactor** (cleanup pass): extracted `app/utils/useQueueDnD.js` (all queue-DnD state: refs, `lists` memo,
  `handleMove` with the display→real index mapping, `queueRealIndex`, the scroll-to-current effect) shared by
  both players; deleted the dead `queueBox`/`upNextBox` refs (leftovers from `measureInWindow`); renamed
  `QueueDragRow.js` → `QueueDrag.js` (file holds provider + row) and tidied the provider (dropped redundant
  `key` from registered rows, inlined the up-region helper).
- **QUEUE view sizing (mobile)**: the QUEUE preview reused the album-cover square style (`albumImage`,
  ~310px on a phone, `min/max width & height + aspectRatio`), so it used very little screen. Now it uses
  `{ width: '100%', flex: 1, maxHeight: '70%' }` — full column width (≤500) and grows to available height
  capped at 70% of the container (no overflow on short screens); title/TimeBar/controls drop below it.
  Desktop unchanged (already half-width/full-height).
- **DnD polish** (`QueueDrag.js`): sibling spring stiffened (`friction 7/60` → `friction 10/tension 140` +
  `overshootClamping: true`) so the gap opens and rows snap back without the elastic bounce/overshoot;
  cross-section target switching now has a `±rowHeight/2` hysteresis dead-band around the up-next box
  bottom — the section only flips when the finger clearly crosses, so near-boundary drags no longer flicker
  between Up next/Queue or land at the far edge of the wrong section. Same-section drops stay exact.
- **1:1 drag tracking** (`QueueDrag.js`): the lifted row used `dy − scrollDelta`, so once edge-autoscroll
  engaged the row drifted away from the finger as the list scrolled. Now it follows the finger exactly
  (`setDrag(dy)`); the `scrollDelta` state was removed (autoscroll still scrolls the list under the finger).

