## 2026-08-30 — FIX: background auto-advance reverts index (same song restarts)
- Report: screen off + natural song end -> same song restarts; next must be pressed 2-3x to
  finally advance. No loop enabled.
- Evidence: instrumented the service + playerCore with logger (Playback events, setIndex,
  nextSong, loadSong). logcat revealed: after a natural end, nextSong setIndex 20 + loadSong 20
  succeeded, then `global.song.index` REVERTED to 19; next presses recomputed setIndex 20 and
  RELOADED track 20 (same song restarts) until a 3rd press finally moved.
- Root cause: songReducer's newSong sets `global.song = { ...state, ...action }` USING REACT'S
  STATE SNAPSHOT. Background advances run through the headless service's fakeSongDispatch and
  mutate global.song but never React's snapshot. The next ordinary React dispatch (useEvent's
  PlaybackState -> setState) then merged the STALE snapshot, reverting global.song's already-
  advanced index/songInfo. Any skip during that window reloaded the current track.
- Fix (2 lines + comment):
  1) songReducer: `state = global.song ?? state` at the top — every transition computes from the
     canonical global.song, never the stale snapshot. React's snapshot lags global.song only, so
     global.song is always the correct base. This kills the revert for good.
  2) servicePlayback: new getSongDispatch() = global.songDispatch || fakeSongDispatch — when the
     app is alive, background advances dispatch to the REAL React reducer, so UI (and global.song)
     move together; fake dispatch stays as cold-headless fallback.
- Instrumentation kept (Settings -> Logs / logcat) pending user's on-device verdict.
- Installed: connected phone only (tablet R52Y80837NY offline).
